  "contracts": [
    "digest hashes the observed Item text; container_digest independently hashes bounded HTTP body bytes exposed by net/http. Prefix hashes never claim complete responses or raw wire streams.",
    "Container origin follows last accepted content response, including redirects/retries; no ETag, deployment revision or original source authenticity is invented.",
    "Raw SARIF request locators omit credentials/query; synthetic web+http(s) view URIs separate extracted script/state and duplicate or inline source-map entries.",
    "Private request selectors remain in keyed report/index identity only. Display paths, text selection, same-origin fetch policy, bounds and content dedup remain established behavior.",
    "Derived occurrence IDs include container digest. Secret/value identity remains independent of source/response.",
    "Decoded state or regex/meta fragments cannot invent verifier/auditor companions; unaltered complete script and declared source-map content retain existing safe binding behavior.",
    "A winning rule replacing a builtin inherits the unbound-view flag, including mobile printable strings.",
    "Discovery acquisition resets parent provenance, source locator and prior response/view context; errors carry safe text/path and no invented content digest."
  ],
